{
  "Water. Cold water, and a voice somewhere above it.": "",
  "Narrator": "",
  "Breathe. Come on. Breathe, blast you.": "",
  "There. Back among the living. The lake doesn't give things back, you know. Not usually.": "",
  "Up you get. Slowly. When you can walk, come and find me by my tent.": "",
  "Hear ye! By order of the Lady Isolde Vane, Steward of Corvalis and Hand of the late King!": "",
  "Ten thousand crowns to whoever brings Her Majesty Queen Victoria out of the wizard's tower! Ten thousand crowns!": "",
  "Ten thousand crowns. And not one of the Steward's soldiers north of Ashford.": "",
  "A villager": "",
  "Bar your doors at sunset. That's all the Steward ever sends us. Bounties and advice.": "",
  "Another villager": "",
  "Somewhere above the village a bell begins to toll.": "",
  "Wrong, somehow. Each stroke swells up out of silence and stops dead, as if the sound were being sucked back into the bronze.": "",
  "In the churchyard, the earth heaves.": "",
  "Inside! Everyone inside! Bar the doors!": "",
  "Under the cracked bell, an old man in a sexton's coat hauls on a rope that is not there.": "",
  "Late... late for the knell... the King is dead... the King is dead...": "",
  "The Bell-Ringer": "El Campanero",
  "He turns. There is black lace knotted round his arm.": "",
  "She hears... every bell...": "",
  "The bell gives one last crack, and is silent.": "",
  "What did he have on his arm? Show me. Lace. Black lace.": "",
  "That's from a wedding veil. Hers was white. Her mother's veil, Elowen's. I took up the hem myself, the night before.": "",
  "That monster tore it up and gave it to his creatures. Like a favour. Like she was his to give.": "",
  "Nan turns the lace over in her hands for a long time, and says nothing more.": "",
  "ACT I COMPLETE": "",
  "A girl with a bow on her back is sitting on the mill step, glaring at the river as if it owes her money.": "",
  "You're the ones who climbed the bell tower. Mam says you went to Aldric for her.": "",
  "Seven years he knew where they found my brother's cloak. Seven years.": "",
  "You're going to take me to him.": "",
  "You found his cloak. And you told my mother NOTHING.": "",
  "I did.": "",
  "Why?": "",
  "Because I didn't know who did it, and I knew exactly who'd go looking. A girl of ten, with a bow taller than she was.": "",
  "The Weeping Bridge is up the Lisle, deep in the Weepwood. The Wardens' old crossing.": "",
  "That last year, he spent his evenings at the hollow oak on the west shore. I thought he was watching the lake.": "",
  "Wren says nothing. Her knuckles are white on her bow.": "",
  "A crow sits on the old oak, watching the water. As you come near it lifts off and flies north without a sound.": "",
  "Crows. They're everywhere since the bells.": "",
  "Black crow, quill down. 'I'm coming.'": "",
  "It's fresh. It hasn't even been rained on. Nobody knows this code but him, and her, and Aldric.": "",
  "She looks out at the lake for a long time.": "",
  "So who's coming?": "",
  "Nobody answers. Out on the Mirror, nothing moves.": "",
  "Under the thorns the river runs black and quiet.": "",
  "The willows have gone black, their branches ending in thorns. Pale spikes of bone grow up between the roots. The light comes down green and dim.": "",
  "It wasn't like this in the spring. It was just a wood. I used to sleep in it.": "",
  "Stay on the path, and if you see lights in the trees, don't follow them.": "",
  "The King's Chase. Wider glades, older oaks gone black, and everywhere the remains of royal order: boundary stones with the crown cut on them, a ride cut dead straight through the trees for horses.": "",
  "His Chase. Anyone caught taking his deer was hanged. I've taken forty.": "",
  "The Lisle runs wide and slow and black here. The bone spikes stand taller, and the light is the colour of pond water.": "",
  "Heron Reach. The Wardens kept this river for a hundred years. Look at it.": "",
  "Down at the ford, figures in rusted livery walk up and down, up and down, searching the road.": "",
  "Smoke, and a ring of glowing mounds in a clearing. Faces behind them.": "",
  "That's close enough. We don't open the ring after dusk. Not for anyone.": "",
  "Hesketh Coll. You used to give my brother bread.": "",
  "A long pause.": "",
  "Ashdown's girl?": "",
  "Figures come out of the trees, black as the kilns, and walk toward them without hurrying.": "",
  "That's Col. That's Col Brenner. I buried him myself.": "",
  "Then bury him again.": "",
  "Hesketh puts a tarnished Warden badge in Wren's hand, and a logbook in yours.": "",
  "Every week, regular as frost. Last time, he gave me these. Badge and book.": "",
  "'If I'm not back by the new moon, give them to Aldric. Tell him I'm sorry, and that I've gone where he'd have gone, if he were young and stupid.'": "",
  "I didn't know where Aldric's camp was. The Wardens were gone. And the riders said the boy ran south.": "",
  "Wren takes the badge and doesn't say anything for a long time.": "",
  "Far off between the willows, a lantern, swinging like someone walking. Going north.": "",
  "That's no wisp. Wisps don't swing.": "",
  "It stops, as if whoever carries it has turned to look at you. Then it goes out.": "",
  "Every pen open, the doors chewed through from the inside.": "",
  "These were the King's hounds. The bone hounds in Millbrook's fields. They came from here.": "",
  "Wren sets the kennels alight and watches them burn.": "",
  "The ropes creak, though there is no wind.": "",
  "One by one, the hanged let go of the branch.": "",
  "On a stone seat at the end of the hall an old chieftain lifts his antlered helm from his knees, and puts it on.": "",
  "Who wakes us?": "",
  "The Thane under the Hill": "El Thane bajo la Colina",
  "The singer put us to sleep. Five hundred winters, under her song. Now the song runs backwards.": "",
  "Someone wears her crown with a cold heart.": "",
  "She sang. Not him... not the sellsword. She...": "",
  "He lies down on his seat and is still.": "",
  "The wizard. Who else wears it?": "",
  "The roll of the Wardens of the Lisle, cut into the beam over the hearth in forty hands. One name has been hacked out with an axe, and THIEF carved over the splinters.": "",
  "Wren takes out her knife and cuts it back, letter by letter: MARCIAN ASHDOWN.": "",
  "There. Let them come and scratch it out again.": "",
  "\"He said I was too old for a nurse. I think he meant I was too old to be loved by anyone but him.\"": "",
  "I fought them on the stair. Did she know that? I bit one of them. Sixty-seven years old and I bit a grown man.": "",
  "She is quiet a while.": "",
  "She thought I let them take me. When you bring her home, I'll tell her myself.": "",
  "Nan turns the pages slowly.": "",
  "The Queen's Day. That's what the court called it, for the old queen.": "",
  "It was my girl's birthday too. Nobody ever called it that.": "",
  "She'd sit in the window of the south tower all day and watch the road for the hunt to come home. And when it came, he'd go straight past her.": "",
  "Two great black willows, an old stone bridge, and in the middle of it a knight in rusted royal armour, hands folded on his sword.": "",
  "Halt. No one crosses. By order of the King.": "",
  "Sir Garrick Thorne": "Sir Garrick Thorne",
  "The King's dead, you tin can.": "",
  "Black lace is knotted round his sword arm.": "",
  "He goes down on one knee and lowers his sword, for the first time in seven years.": "",
  "Seven years I've stood on this bridge. You want to know what happened here. I tell the river every night. It never answers.": "",
  "The King had a letter put in the boy's hands. In her writing: the Weeping Bridge, at moonrise. She never wrote it. I don't know whose pen it was. I didn't ask.": "",
  "He came at moonrise, the Warden boy, smiling, with a ring in his fist. The wizard was waiting under the bridge. Roots came up out of the bank and held him.": "",
  "He blew his whistle. The Warden call. Nobody came. And the King sat his horse on the bank, and watched, and said, 'Now.'": "",
  "It was my sword.": "",
  "We gave him to the old gravedigger at the fens, with orders to sink him. I kept his whistle. I don't know why.": "",
  "Then they made me her jailer. Seven years at the top of the stair with the key on my belt. I heard what he did to her behind that door. Every time. And afterwards I turned the key.": "",
  "She sang, the first year. Through the door. Then she stopped.": "",
  "Tell her I'm sorry. I should have let her run. And the grey thing at her window, every night, the year before the thorns. I should have shot it.": "",
  "He holds out a small bone whistle, yellow with age.": "",
  "Wren nocks an arrow and draws it to her ear, aimed at the knight's heart.": "",
  "Look at me.": "",
  "He looks at her. She looses; the arrow goes through him and clatters on the stones.": "",
  "Of course. You're already dead. You don't even get to die.": "",
  "The King's dead too. That leaves one. The next one's for the wizard.": "",
  "The fens. They put him in the fens. When this is done, I'm going to find him.": "",
  "Mam. He didn't run. They killed him at the bridge. The King, and the wizard, and a knight with a sword.": "",
  "Maud is quiet for a long time.": "",
  "I know, love. I've always known. I only needed someone to say it.": "",
  "She goes to the window, and for a moment it looks as if she'll blow the lamp out. She turns the wick up instead.": "",
  "It's for you now. For all of you, going north. Come home.": "",
  "ACT II COMPLETE": "",
  "A slime. It has not noticed you.": "",
  "Scenes can talk, move the camera, set flags and hand you things.": "",
  "SCENE OVER": "",
  "Victoria's diary": "El diario de Victoria",
  "Letters": "Cartas",
  "Proclamations": "Proclamas",
  "Notes": "Notas",
  "Black lace": "Encaje negro",
  "The Hollow King's proclamation": "La proclama del Rey Hueco",
  "Nailed to the board by Aldric's camp": "",
  "BY THE GRACE OF THE CROWN OF DAWN.": "",
  "Be it known to every soul in Corvalis that Osric, third of that name, is dead; that his daughter Victoria is Queen; and that her lawful husband, Ambrose of the Root Tower, holds the realm in her name as King.": "",
  "The dead walk because the realm has strayed. Let every door be barred at sunset. Let no one go north. Let no one come for her.": "",
  "Ambrose, King.": "",
  "And below it, in a small, fine hand: Victoria R.": "",
  "The Steward's bounty": "La recompensa de la Senescal",
  "The herald's board, Millbrook square": "",
  "By order of the Lady Isolde Vane, Steward of Corvalis and Hand of the late King:": "",
  "TEN THOUSAND CROWNS to whoever brings Her Majesty Queen Victoria out of the tower of Thornhallow, and the false king Ambrose to justice.": "",
  "Proof of the deed to be brought to the Steward at Ashford.": "",
  "A page of a diary": "Una página de un diario",
  "Nan Merrow: \"It blew down the Lisle on the night wind.\"": "",
  "A boy pulled me out of the lake today. He had duckweed in his hair and he laughed at me the whole way home. He never asked who I was.": "",
  "I'm going back tomorrow to thank him. That's all. Just to thank him.": "",
  "A second page": "Una segunda página",
  "Nan Merrow": "Nan Merrow",
  "A grey goose feather in the oak today. That means tomorrow.": "",
  "Marcian says a Warden can read a whole letter in a pocketful of feathers. I said a princess could write one.": "",
  "A third page": "Una tercera página",
  "Father has sold me. The price was a war, and the buyer is the wizard they call Potatoe Face.": "",
  "I told Father I will marry Marcian or no one. He said, \"Then no one will have Marcian.\"": "",
  "I didn't understand what he meant.": "",
  "To the King, at Castle Corvane": "Al Rey, en el Castillo Corvane",
  "Left on a doorstep in Millbrook, at night. The seal is unbroken; the paper is seven years old.": "",
  "Dear Father,": "",
  "I will do my duty. I will smile at his feasts and I will sign what I am given. I only ask that Nan may stay with me. Please. She is all I have.": "",
  "Your daughter, Victoria.": "",
  "A scrap of black lace": "Un jirón de encaje negro",
  "Knotted round the Bell-Ringer's arm": "",
  "A torn strip of fine lace, black as soot, tied round the arm the way a knight wears his lady's favour.": "",
  "Deep in the weave, here and there, a thread is still white.": "",
  "Marcian's feather key": "La llave de pluma de Marcian",
  "The hollow oak, wrapped in a Warden's oilskin": "",
  "For V., so you can read me when I'm late, and read the trail when you come to find me.": "",
  "Grey goose: tomorrow (on a trail, onward). Owl: tonight, at moonrise (on a trail, shelter). Heron: at our bridge (on a trail, the crossing). Jay: don't come, there are people about (on a trail, danger, go round).": "",
  "Swan's down: yes. Two feathers crossed: always. Black crow, quill down: I'm coming.": "",
  "Burn this. (You won't.) M.": "",
  "A note signed V.": "Una nota firmada «V.»",
  "The hollow oak": "",
  "Owl feather found. Moonrise, then. I'll bring the bread if you bring the stars.": "",
  "And a better song: your last one frightened the ducks.": "",
  "V.": "",
  "Another note signed V.": "Otra nota firmada «V.»",
  "The hollow oak, at the bottom: the last thing she left": "",
  "They say you robbed the treasury and ran. I know you didn't.": "",
  "If you're hiding, I'll wait. If you're dead, I'll find you.": "",
  "A black crow feather": "Una pluma negra de cuervo",
  "The hollow oak, on top of everything": "",
  "Fresh and glossy, laid quill-down. The rain hasn't touched it.": "",
  "In Marcian's key, a black crow, quill down, means: I'm coming.": "",
  "Marcian's logbook": "El libro de rondas de Marcian",
  "Left with Hesketh Coll at Kilnholt, \"in case\"": "",
  "The round of the Lisle. Marcian Ashdown, Warden.": "",
  "Spring, the 3rd. Wolves at the Chase edge, two. Jay recut at the spider dell. Bread at Kilnholt; Mother Dunn says I'm too thin. The children made me sing. The ducks left.": "",
  "The 17th. Gallows Willow: the foresters have hanged a man for a hare. Cut him down and buried him. Will hear about it.": "",
  "The 24th. Asked Aldric if a Warden may marry. He laughed and said a Warden may do as he likes, so long as the fire is kept. Bought iron for a ring.": "",
  "The marks of the round, for whoever walks it after me: a goose by the river camp, a jay at the dell, a goose on the old road above Kilnholt, the owl over the lodge door, the heron at the ford, and the last at the mist.": "",
  "The last. A letter from V. Her own hand, but not through the oak, which she has never once done. The bridge, at moonrise. Odd. I'm going anyway. Badge and book to Hesketh, in case.": "",
  "The roll of the Wardens": "La lista de los Guardianes",
  "Heron Lodge, the beam over the hearth": "",
  "The Wardens of the Lisle, cut into the beam in forty hands, the oldest worn almost smooth. Edric. Aldric. Forty names in all.": "",
  "One has been hacked out with an axe and THIEF carved over the splinters.": "",
  "Wren cut it back, letter by letter: MARCIAN ASHDOWN.": "",
  "The King's game book": "El libro de caza del Rey",
  "The King's hunting lodge, on the table": "",
  "Page after page in the foresters' hand, one hunt a year, always on the same day.": "",
  "The Queen's Day. The King rides out at dawn with the hounds, Bellow, Grief, Old Tally and Bramble. A hart and two boar. The King does not speak.": "",
  "Year after year, the same. The Queen's Day. The King rides out at dawn, though the princess asked to come.": "",
  "Twenty-five of them. The last: The Queen's Day. No hunt. The King keeps to his bed.": "",
  "The Steward's dispatch": "El despacho de la Senescal",
  "Pike's courier's bag, from the outriders' chief": "",
  "From the Steward, to Sergeant Pike at Millbrook.": "",
  "Pay out no bounty without proof. If Her Majesty is found, she is to be brought to Ashford by night, under guard, and spoken to by no one. No one, Sergeant.": "",
  "Burn this. I. V.": "",
  "The search party's orders": "Las órdenes de la partida de búsqueda",
  "On the sergeant of the search party. The paper is seven years old.": "",
  "The lady has left her room by the window. Search the Weepwood road as far as the river.": "",
  "She is to be back in her room before my lord wakes, or it will go worse for her.": "",
  "Crane, steward.": "",
  "A fourth page": "Una cuarta página",
  "Caught on the thorns in the Weepwood": "",
  "They say Marcian robbed the treasury and ran south. He wouldn't. He wouldn't. He would NOT.": "",
  "I am to be married on Saturday. I will wear Mother's veil, so that at least one person there loves me.": "",
  "A fifth page": "Una quinta página",
  "Caught on the thorns in the Weepwood. \"Thornhallow, the first autumn.\"": "",
  "I would not smile at his guests tonight, so he struck me, there at the table, in front of all of them. Lady Mirabel laughed behind her fan.": "",
  "Afterwards he stood outside my door and cried, and in the morning there was a new gown on my bed. I don't know which part frightened me more.": "",
  "A sixth page": "Una sexta página",
  "Caught on the thorns at Heron Reach. \"The first winter.\"": "",
  "He sent Nan away today. He said I was too old for a nurse. I think he meant I was too old to be loved by anyone but him.": "",
  "I wrote to Father. I will write every week until he answers.": "",
  "A seventh page": "Una séptima página",
  "Caught on the thorns by the road past the mist. \"The second year.\"": "",
  "I got as far as the Weepwood. I could smell the lake. Sir Garrick carried me back like a sack of flour and would not look at me.": "",
  "Three days now with no candle and no supper. They are bricking up my window. I can still see one stripe of sky.": "",
  "I am going to stop singing now. There's no one left to hear it but him.": "",
  "To Nan Merrow, Millbrook": "A Nan Merrow, Millbrook",
  "Left on the mill's doorstep at night: the wrong door (Nan's is next along). The seal is unbroken.": "",
  "Nan,": "",
  "he says you were sent away for stealing. I know you never stole anything in your life except cake for me.": "",
  "I will find a way to bring you back. Don't forget me.": "",
  "Left on Heron Lodge's step at night. The second year.": "",
  "Father,": "",
  "they have bricked up my window. I can see one stripe of sky.": "",
  "He hurts me, Father. He hurts me, and then he cries and brings me dresses. I will be good. I will be so good. Please let me come home.": "",
  "The King's bridge": "El puente del Rey",
  "Nailed to the post at the south end of the Weeping Bridge": "",
  "BY ORDER OF THE KING.": "",
  "The Weeping Bridge is closed, now and for ever. Let no one cross it. Let no one fish beneath it, or sing upon it, or stop there to rest. Whoever is found upon it shall be held there until the river runs dry.": "",
  "Ambrose, King. The letters wander, as if the pen had been very heavy.": "",
  "And below, small and fine and dark, pressed so hard the nib has torn the paper: Victoria R.": "",
  "Grey dust and a dead moth": "Polvo gris y una polilla muerta",
  "Where the lantern went out, in the Weepwood": "",
  "Where the lantern went out there are no footprints, only a drift of fine grey dust on the moss, like ash from a cold fire,": "",
  "and a dead moth as big as your hand.": "",
  "A second scrap of black lace": "Un segundo jirón de encaje negro",
  "Knotted round Sir Garrick's sword arm": "",
  "The same lace as the first, black as soot, a white thread here and there deep in the weave.": "",
  "The torn edges match. Two pieces of one veil.": "",
  "A note in the grass": "Una nota en la hierba",
  "Found in the Test Field": "",
  "If you can read this, the journal works.": "",
  "Nothing else is written here.": ""
}
